From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:07:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(linux): build the Linux AppImage in a reproducible
 container

Add docker/Dockerfile and docker/Makefile defining the Linux build
environment (the build-linux apt-deps.txt packages plus SDL2/tinyxml2/libzip
built from source, frozen into image layers) and rewire the build-linux job
to produce its AppImage with `make -C docker appimage`.

The container mirrors the job's ubuntu-22.04 / gcc-12 environment exactly; the
only intended change is freezing the from-source library steps into image
layers, so the build is reproducible and a developer can run the identical
build locally. The generate-2ship-otr job and the uploaded artifact are
unchanged: the job still downloads 2ship.o2r into build-cmake/mm, where the
build bundles it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
